    {
      "text": "Cross‑contact with gluten‑containing foods should be prevented by keeping gluten‑free foods separate from foods that contain wheat, barley, or rye.",
      "sources": [2]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even foods that seem safe, like oats, should only be eaten if they are labeled gluten‑free because oats can be contaminated with gluten during processing.",
      "sources": [3]
    }
  ]
}

{
